<article class="env-remark" id="0F4I">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F4I">Remark <span data-tag="0F4I">23.6.4</span>.</a> We can also adjoin a set (possibly infinite) of exterior or divided power generators in a given degree $d > 0$, rather than just one as in Examples <a href="/tag/09PH" data-tag="09PH">23.6.2</a> and <a href="/tag/09PI" data-tag="09PI">23.6.3</a>. Namely, following Remark <a href="/tag/07H6" data-tag="07H6">23.5.2</a>: for $(A,\gamma )$ as above and a set $J$, let $A\langle T_ j:j\in J\rangle $ be the directed colimit of the algebras $A\langle T_ j:j\in S\rangle $ over all finite subsets $S$ of $J$. It is immediate that this algebra has a unique divided power structure, compatible with the given structure on $A$ and on each generator $T_ j$. </p>
</article>